        <title type="html"><![CDATA[add allow-type to npm as an aggregate for allow-git, etc]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/npm/statusboard/issues/1064</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/npm/statusboard/issues/1064"/>
        <updated>2026-02-18T16:35:03.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36607?u=79d8c114db476a7ecc6328b328f71d9d758368c7&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Epic</h3>
<p dir="auto">pacote supports <code class="notranslate">allow-git</code> <code class="notranslate">allow-remote</code>, etc to limit fetching from non-registry endpoints.  npm needs an aggregate flag so folks can configure them in one place.</p>
<p dir="auto">This will be <code class="notranslate">--allow-type</code> with the values being a loose mapping to npm-package-arg types (registry will be an analog for version/range/tag).</p>]]></content>
